      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 603</b></color></size>

    <b>Madhubani painting</b>

    <size=74%>A living tradition

    <i>Natural pigments on paper</i>

    Various collections</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    For generations women in the Mithila region of Bihar painted the walls of their homes with gods, nature and wedding scenes in bold lines and bright colours. After a drought in the 1960s the art moved onto paper and became an important source of income.</size>

    <size=50%><color=#8A8A8A>Photo: Rohini / CC BY-SA 3.0 / Wikimedia Commons</color></size>'
