      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 606</b></color></size>

    <b>Ashoka''s inscriptions and the decipherment of Brahmi</b>

    <size=74%>Edicts c. 260 BCE; script deciphered 1837

    <i>Inscription carved in stone</i>

    In situ, Girnar, Junagadh</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    For centuries no one could read the inscriptions on Ashoka''s pillars and rocks. In 1837 James Prinsep, building on the work of many scholars, deciphered the Brahmi script, the ancestor of most South and South-East Asian scripts. A forgotten emperor spoke again.</size>

    <size=50%><color=#8A8A8A>Photo: Alexander Cunningham, Eugen Hultzsch Date=1877 / Public domain / Wikimedia Commons</color></size>'
